  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Tennessee recorded $1.2B in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. The state received 754 awards with an average award size of $1.6M, and obligations fell 90.6% year over year. Fiscal-year history shows much larger annual totals in recent years: FY22 $11.5B, FY23 $11.3B, FY24 $10.8B, FY25 $11.1B, and FY26 $12.5B. The Department of Energy accounted for the largest share of FY2027 to date obligations at $968M, followed by the Department of Veterans Affairs at $148M and the Department of Justice at $41M. CONSOLIDATED NUCLEAR SECURITY, LLC led vendors with $489M, followed by UT-BATTELLE LLC with $302M and UNITED CLEANUP OAK RIDGE LLC with $113M. Facilities Support Services dominated industry spending in FY2027 to date at $798M, with Remediation Services at $113M and Other Basic Inorganic Chemical Manufacturing at $68M. These figures reflect partial fiscal-year totals and should be read as fiscal year to date obligations, not full-year results.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Why are FY2027 to date obligations much lower than prior fiscal years?",
        "body": "The comparison shows a steep year-over-year decline: obligations fell 90.6% year over year. Fiscal-year totals before FY27 were in the $10.8B to $12.5B range, while FY27 to date is $1.2B. The Department of Energy concentrated much of the FY27 to date spending with $968M, which shapes the current distribution of obligations."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies, vendors, and industries are driving FY2027 to date spending?",
        "body": "The Department of Energy is the top buyer with $968M, followed by the Department of Veterans Affairs at $148M and the Department of Justice at $41M. CONSOLIDATED NUCLEAR SECURITY, LLC received $489M, UT-BATTELLE LLC received $302M, and UNITED CLEANUP OAK RIDGE LLC received $113M. Facilities Support Services is the largest industry by obligations at $798M, with Remediation Services at $113M and Other Basic Inorganic Chemical Manufacturing at $68M."
      }
    ]
  },
